      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:81:6",
      "text": [
        " لَا بَأْسَ بِأَنْ تُلَبِّيَ وَ أَنْتَ عَلَى غَيْرِ طُهْرٍ وَ عَلَى كُلِّ حَالٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali, from his father, from Hammad Bin Usman, from Al Halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘There is no problem with it if you were to exclaim <span class=\"iTxt\">Talbiyya</span> upon other than purity, and upon every state’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Ali has narrated from his father from Hammad ibn ‘Uthaman from al-Halabiy who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘It is not harmful to say Talbiyah without Tahur (cleansing, with wudu’ or Ghusl (bath)) in all conditions.’” "
        ]
      }
